From 6a2da94b640de82b70941c90849f272c1cdbfeda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitry B <dimitryB@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:37:27 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/30] facilitator: register the bip122 chain and
 v2-bip122-exact

Adds Bitcoin networks (CAIP-2 namespace bip122) to the facilitator
binary, behind the feature chain-bip122. The scheme is the crate
x402-chain-bip122.

- config.rs: a "bip122:<genesis hash prefix>" key reads the chain's
  configuration: the Hemi chain that records its payments, the
  X402BtcSettler address, and the confirmation policy.
- chain.rs: ChainProvider::Bip122. The registry is built in two passes:
  every chain with its own provider first, then each Bitcoin chain from
  the provider of the Hemi chain it names. That provider is shared, not
  rebuilt: a second provider for the same signer would have its own nonce
  manager, so a BTC and a USDC.e settlement could take the same nonce.
  A Bitcoin chain whose Hemi chain is not configured is a startup error.
  One whose settler address is unset or empty is skipped with a warning,
  so a config can list the Bitcoin chains before the contract exists.
- schemes.rs, run.rs: V2Bip122Exact is built from that provider and
  registered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
